Package: usb-lcd-dashboard
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: USB LCD Dashboard <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-pil (>= 10.1), python3-serial (>= 3.5),
 python3-numpy, fonts-dejavu-core
Recommends: systemd, git, fonts-ubuntu
Homepage: https://github.com/smartguy05/usb-lcd
Description: Live Claude Code and Codex dashboard for a USB LCD panel
 Drives a Turing/UsbMonitor 3.5-inch USB LCD as a status display for Claude
 Code and Codex sessions, showing the provider, model, project, elapsed time,
 permission requests and context used. It never displays prompts, responses or
 transcript text — only lifecycle metadata.
 .
 The panel is divided into tiles, each holding a widget: a clock, an agent
 card, or an animated crab that changes expression with what the agent is
 doing and waves both claws when it needs your attention.
 .
 Installing this package puts the program and its udev rule in place. Wiring it
 into your own Claude and Codex sessions is a per-user step: run
 "usb-lcd-dashboard install" as yourself, which merges the hooks and enables a
 systemd user service.
 .
 fonts-dejavu-core is a hard dependency rather than a recommendation: a minimal
 Ubuntu ships no TrueType font at all, and the panel would silently fall back to
 a bitmap face on a device whose whole purpose is legible text.
